# XSH pthread_cancel()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Cancellation is processed asynchronously to the caller and no bound is
# set on how soon it is acted on: each test polls for its effects for up
# to 10 s and joins through a helper thread, so a thread that never
# ends gives a FAIL rather than a hang.

assertion  XSH.pthread_cancel.001
anchor     functions/pthread_cancel.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/pthread_cancel.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.9.5.2
class      required
since      2008
says       pthread_cancel() of a thread (cancelability enabled and
           deferred, the defaults) blocked in read() of an empty pipe
           returns 0; the thread does not return from read(), runs its
           cleanup handler, and pthread_join() gives PTHREAD_CANCELED.
test       t/001-blocked-read.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_cancel.002
anchor     functions/pthread_cancel.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.9.5.3
class      required
since      2008
says       A canceled thread with a cleanup handler pushed and a non-NULL
           thread-specific value runs the handler, then the key's
           destructor (with that value), and only then terminates:
           pthread_join() returns PTHREAD_CANCELED after both have run.
test       t/002-order.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_cancel.003
anchor     functions/pthread_cancel.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.9.5.3
class      required
since      2024
says       pthread_cancel() of a thread that has returned from its start
           routine but has not been joined returns 0, and pthread_join()
           then gives the value the thread returned.
note       The thread is given 200 ms to terminate; had it not, it has
           no cancellation point left, so the outcome is the same.
test       t/003-zombie.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_cancel.004
anchor     functions/pthread_cancel.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       pthread_cancel() returns 0 while its target has cancelability
           disabled and is waiting for that call to return; the target
           then enables cancelability and is canceled at
           pthread_testcancel().
test       t/004-asynchronous.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_cancel.005
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.9.5.3
class      required
since      2008
says       A cleanup handler run while a cancellation is acted on finds
           the cancelability state PTHREAD_CANCEL_DISABLE and the type
           PTHREAD_CANCEL_DEFERRED (pthread_setcancelstate(DISABLE) and
           pthread_setcanceltype(DEFERRED) report them as previous), the
           thread having set PTHREAD_CANCEL_ASYNCHRONOUS.
note       The thread spins for 3 s after the request with the type
           ASYNCHRONOUS and then reaches pthread_testcancel() as DEFERRED,
           so the test holds whether or not an asynchronous request is
           acted on at once (XSH.pthread_setcancelstate.006); the type is
           checked only on systems that do. The fault planted is a
           request never made; the state and type change itself happens
           inside the implementation's cancellation processing, which a
           preload library cannot reach, and is reviewed by hand.
test       t/005-acting-disables.c
